From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI recents: no gradient above the navigation bar

Recents draws recents_lower_gradient above the navigation bar whenever it has
tasks. On the device (Test V40) it shows as a band 45 px high going from white
to grey 243 just above the white navigation bar: on 16 grey levels a gradient
is a step, and it is drawn on every opening of recents
(docs/design/eink-ui.md, rule 5: no gradients). The view stays (the scrim code
finds and animates it), with nothing in it, as the device overlay does for
the corresponding scrim of quick settings (qs_navbar_scrim.xml).

--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/recents.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/recents.xml
@@ -40,5 +40,5 @@
         android:layout_height="wrap_content"
         android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal|bottom"
         android:scaleType="fitXY"
-        android:src="@drawable/recents_lower_gradient" />
+        android:src="@android:color/transparent" />
 </FrameLayout>
